    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a7">

                <pb facs="0270" n="264" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg264"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Cologan to Count von Waldersee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-03-26"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Marechal</hi>: The diplomatic corps has
                    read with great pleasure the letter of your excellency dated the 25th of this
                    month, and bearing No. 1154. It has seen the agreement with you on the methods
                    to be followed to continue as rapidly as possible the works for the improvement
                    of navigation on the Peiho; it has decided to give as instructions to the
                    consuls at Tientsin, who on their side had submitted the question to it, to
                    reach an understanding with the provisional government to form the committee to
                    which your letter alludes, to fix the powers of its members, and to prosecute
                    the carrying out of the scheme in question.</p>
                <p>As to defining the powers of the provisional government, and as to the
                    regulations which your excellency was pleased to send me with the letter to
                    which I am now replying, the diplomatic corps reserves to itself to inform you
                    shortly of the manner in which they should be understood.</p>
                <p>I inclose with this letter the documents sent in your communication of the 13th
                    March, and which you have asked me to return to you.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
